<title>USA: World Bank approves $22 mln Poland loan.</title>
<headline>World Bank approves $22 mln Poland loan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank on Thursday approved a $22 million loan to help strengthen municipal management and financing in Poland, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>The bank said the project backed by the loan would help improve local authorities' access to commercial loans to finance infrastructure investments.</p>
<p>In the long run this should &quot;enhance urban efficiency and living standards&quot;, it added.</p>
</text>
